From b4ce4a26065d0674a6da90be684d5ebd1dc8a192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:59:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] proxy/pf: honour externalTrafficPolicy and
 internalTrafficPolicy: Local

The pf proxier redirected a Service's ClusterIP and NodePorts to one set of
endpoints, allLocallyReachableEndpoints, which ignores the traffic
policies. With externalTrafficPolicy: Local, external NodePort traffic
was still sent to endpoints on other nodes, masqueraded to the node's
address so the client address was lost, and a node without a local
endpoint accepted the traffic instead of dropping it. With
internalTrafficPolicy: Local, ClusterIP traffic still reached remote
endpoints.

Give each kind of traffic its own target, as the iptables proxier does:
- ClusterIP: the internal endpoints (internalTrafficPolicy).
- NodePort from outside: the external endpoints (externalTrafficPolicy).
  With Local this is local endpoints only, unmasqueraded; with no local
  endpoint the traffic is dropped.
- NodePort from pods (the local traffic detector's cluster CIDR) and from
  the node itself, with externalTrafficPolicy: Local: short-circuited to
  the cluster-wide endpoints.

Each target picks its own port group. The choice among port groups of
equal size is now deterministic (lowest port) instead of map order.
